      "description": "Liaobin Tower was built in the tenth year of Qiantong (1110) and completed in the fourth year of Tianqing (1114) (from the Tiangong inscription records)\n.\nIn Liaobin Village, 29 kilometers northeast of Xinmin City, there are the remains of a thousand-year-old city. This ancient city is located at the intersection of the Liao River and the Xiushui River. It was a famous ferry and transportation artery in ancient times, and was also a battleground for military strategists. Liaobin Tower is an octagonal 13-story green brick tower with dense eaves. The original height is 41.7 meters and the bottom diameter is 12.5 meters.\nThe original material is provided by Xiaolu（小绿）, the blogger of Xiaohongshu."
